// Language section: Strings.
page strings { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Strings" {}

  text {
    span "String literals are UTF-8 by default. A prefix selects another encoding; heredocs offer multi-line and verbatim variants; a `$` prefix opts the string into expression interpolation." {}
  }

  h2 "Literals" {}

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
name  = "hello"          // utf8 (default)
label = utf8"hello"      // explicit
tag   = ascii"id-007"
wide  = utf16"hello"
quad  = utf32"hello"
WCL
  }

  h2 "Escapes" {}

  text {
    span "Inside a double-quoted string, the usual escape sequences apply: `\\\\`, `\\\"`, `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`. For backslash-heavy text — regexes, LaTeX, Windows paths — prefer a **raw heredoc** (below)." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
greeting = "Hello,\nworld!"        // newline embedded
quoted   = "She said \"hi\"."
WCL
  }

  h2 "Types" {}

  table {
    rows:
      | "Type"    | "Use" |
      | "`utf8`"  | "Default. Variable-width Unicode in 1–4 byte sequences." |
      | "`ascii`" | "7-bit text; fits one byte per char, no Unicode." |
      | "`utf16`" | "Variable-width, two bytes per BMP code unit." |
      | "`utf32`" | "Fixed-width, four bytes per code point." |
  }

  callout "Encoding is metadata" {
    class = ["note"]
    body  = "The encoding is part of the value's type. A field declared utf8 will reject an ascii literal; widen or convert at the host layer."
  }

  h2 "Plain heredocs" {}

  text {
    span "`<<TAG ... TAG` introduces a heredoc. The body runs until a line matching the closing tag. Escape sequences (`\\n`, `\\\"`, …) are interpreted. Indentation is stripped to match the closing tag's indentation, so heredocs nest comfortably inside indented blocks." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
note = <<END
First line.
Second line.
END
WCL
  }

  h2 "Raw heredocs" {}

  text {
    span "A **raw heredoc** uses a single-quoted opening tag and takes the body verbatim — no escapes, no interpolation, just literal bytes. Ideal for LaTeX, regexes, code samples with backslashes, or anything where you don't want WCL touching the contents." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
regex = <<'RAW'
\d{3}-\d{4}
RAW

latex = <<'TEX'
\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
TEX
WCL
  }

  callout "Indentation stripping still applies" {
    class = ["tip"]
    body  = "Even in a raw heredoc, the common leading whitespace (matching the closing tag's indent) is stripped from every line. Both forms behave the same way here — only escape handling differs."
  }

  h2 "Interpolation" {}

  text {
    span "Interpolation is opt-in: prefix the string literal with `$`. Inside a `$\"…\"` (or `$<<TAG`), `${ … }` slots evaluate any expression and splice the result into the string. Without the prefix, `${…}` is literal text — no hidden interpolation." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
greeting = $"Hello, ${name}! Count: ${count + 1u32}"

block = $<<MSG
You have ${len(items)} items waiting.
The first is ${head(items)}.
MSG
WCL
  }

  text {
    span "All four encodings accept the `$` prefix (`$\"…\"` / `$ascii\"…\"` / `$utf16\"…\"` / `$utf32\"…\"`)." {}
  }

  text {
    span "Next: [Booleans](booleans)." {}
  }
}
